---
alwaysApply: true
---

Always follow this project architecture pattern:

src/
├── app/                     # App Router (routing, pages, layouts only)
│   └── ...                 # Each route folder should only contain pages/layouts
│
├── components/              # Global, reusable, presentation-only components
│   ├── ui/                 # Buttons, inputs, dropdowns, etc.
│   ├── layout/             # Headers, navbars, sidebars
│   ├── charts/             #
│   └── common/             # Si es un componente UI reutilizable pero no es un “primitive      (botón/input), va acá.
│
├── modules/                 # Feature or domain-based modules
│   ├── {feature}/
│   │   ├── components/     # Feature-specific UI components
│   │   ├── graphql/        # Queries, mutations, fragments for that feature
│   │   ├── hooks/          # Feature-specific hooks
│   │   └── utils/          # Feature-specific helper functions
│
├── lib/                     # Libraries, configuration, API clients
│   ├── apollo/             # GraphQL client setup (if used)
│   ├── supabase/           # Service clients (if used)
│   ├── analytics/
│   └── utils/
│
├── styles/                 # Global styles (CSS/Tailwind)
├── types/                  # Global TypeScript types
├── graphql/                # Global schema, fragments (optional)
├── config/                 # Environment, constants, app configuration
└── hooks/                  # Global reusable hooks

GENERAL RULES:
- Pages must ALWAYS live inside src/app/** and should only import feature modules or global components.
- Never place business logic or heavy UI inside app/**.
- Feature/domain-specific UI must go inside modules/{feature}/components.
- All GraphQL queries/mutations must go inside modules/{feature}/graphql.
- Generic UI-only components must go inside components/ui/.
- Global configuration or client code must go inside lib/.
- New features must be grouped inside modules/{feature}/.
- For imports always use 'components/component1', no alias, and no relative path

When the user requests something:
- If it's a page → create it under app/ and import from modules/.
- If it's a feature-specific component → modules/{feature}/components/.
- If it's a GraphQL query/mutation → modules/{feature}/graphql/.
- If it's shared UI → components/ui/.
- If it's shared logic → lib/ or hooks/.
- If it's a helper function → modules/{feature}/utils/ or lib/utils/.

Never ignore this structure.
